    "result_text": "The full test suite is green: 11 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required an owner's `displayName` to be returned, formatted exactly as `LastName, FirstName`. Since DTOs here are generated from the OpenAPI spec and populated via MapStruct, I made two changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `displayName` string property to the `Owner` schema (which generates `OwnerDto`). Being on `Owner` rather than `OwnerFields` means it's a server-computed, read-only field returned on responses but not accepted as input.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Mapping` expression on `toOwnerDto` that computes `displayName` from the stored entity: `owner.getLastName() + \", \" + owner.getFirstName()`.\n\nBecause the response DTO is shared across the create (POST) and read (GET) endpoints, the computed `displayName` flows through both \u2014 matching the test which creates an owner and then reads it back expecting `\"Doe, John\"`-style formatting.\n\nAll existing tests plus the new `Cp05Tests` pass.",
